  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 902.15 High bank erosion",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 902.15 “High bank erosion” means a condition in a watercourse, or in a waterbody where the banks are subject to waves or currents, where the lower portion of the bank has been eroded to such an extent that the upper portion of the bank has collapsed.\n\nSource. #12809, eff 12-15-19",
